# Culvert Maintenance Agent — sudoers allowlist
#
# This file is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for which `docker compose`
# invocations the agent is allowed to run when privilege_mode=sudoers
# (the production default; see roadmap/D1.6-maintenance-agent-
# implementation-plan.md § 4.5).
#
# The agent's command runner prepends `sudo -n` to every templated
# invocation; sudo's exact-arg matching enforces that the agent cannot
# deviate from this list, even with an in-process bug.
#
# Adding a new operation requires the four-step contract from § 4.6:
#   1. Typed API handler in the agent.
#   2. Command template in internal/runner.
#   3. Sudoers allowlist entries HERE (this file).
#   4. Tests, including the parity test that asserts every runner
#      template has matching lines and vice versa.
#
# Skipping any of the four is a review block.
#
# D1.6a scope: minimal `docker compose ps` entry for /v1/status.
# D1.6b scope: backup (encrypted/unencrypted/list), restore
#   (dryrun/commit, fully enumerated), compose down, compose up -d,
#   cleanup leftovers (dryrun/commit).
# Upgrade check scope: read-only image inspect + manifest inspect for
#   the upgrade-availability check. NO pull, upgrade apply, or rollback
#   yet — those land with their own handlers + entries.
#
# Operator install steps:
#   The recommended path is to run packaging/culvert-maint/install.sh,
#   which reads compose_project_dir and compose_file from
#   /etc/culvert-maint/config.toml, renders the sudoers file with the
#   *full* compose path, runs `visudo -c` to validate, and refuses to
#   complete the install if any placeholder remains.
#
#   For manual installation, replace {compose_path} below with the
#   absolute, joined path:
#       <compose_project_dir>/<compose_file>
#   Then validate with:
#       visudo -c -f /etc/sudoers.d/culvert-maint
#   And install with mode 0440 root:root:
#       install -m 0440 -o root -g root \
#           packaging/sudoers/culvert-maint \
#           /etc/sudoers.d/culvert-maint
#
# IMPORTANT: this file MUST be path-bound. sudo's exact-arg matching
# does NOT honor the agent's process cwd; without the absolute path
# the allowlist would accept the same `docker compose -f X ps` from
# any working directory the agent could be coerced into.
#
# Wildcards (`*`) in this file each match exactly ONE argv token. The
# wildcards live ONLY in argv positions where the agent enforces
# strong validation upstream:
#   - /backup/*  — agent validates the filename matches
#                  ^[a-zA-Z0-9._-]{1,255}$ before sudo is invoked.
#   - --older-than * --keep-last *
#                — agent enforces time.ParseDuration shape with bounds
#                  (1h to 1y) and integer keep_last in 0..100.
#   - image inspect * / manifest inspect --verbose *
#                — agent enforces the operator's image_allowlist regex
#                  (policy) AND a bounded argv-safety shape
#                  (^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._/:@-]{0,511}$, no leading
#                  dash) before sudo is invoked. Both commands are
#                  read-only — they do not mutate the host or the stack.
# Restore-flag combinations (mode + --accept-dp-reenrollment +
# --allow-counter-rollback) are fully ENUMERATED rather than wildcarded:
# 3 modes × 4 flag combinations × 2 templates (dryrun, commit) = 24
# lines. No trailing `*` is used to collapse the enumeration — that
# would broaden the privilege boundary just for readability.
#
# The static parity test
# (cmd/culvert-maint/internal/runner/parity_test.go) asserts the union
# of every Template.SudoersLines exactly matches the entries below: no
# missing, no dead surface.

# ─── compose.status (D1.6a) ─────────────────────────────────────────
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} ps --format json

# ─── compose.cli.backup.* (D1.6b) ───────────────────────────────────
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --encrypt --backup /backup/*
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm cli --backup /backup/*
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm cli --list-backups --backup-dir /backup

# ─── compose.cli.restore.dryrun (D1.6b) ─────────────────────────────
# 3 modes × 4 flag combos = 12 enumerated lines. Canonical argv order:
#   --restore /backup/* --mode <mode>
#   [--accept-dp-reenrollment]
#   [--allow-counter-rollback]
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode full
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode full --accept-dp-reenrollment
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode full --allow-counter-rollback
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode full --accept-dp-reenrollment --allow-counter-rollback
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode trust-root-only
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode trust-root-only --accept-dp-reenrollment
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode trust-root-only --allow-counter-rollback
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode trust-root-only --accept-dp-reenrollment --allow-counter-rollback
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode state-only
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode state-only --accept-dp-reenrollment
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode state-only --allow-counter-rollback
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode state-only --accept-dp-reenrollment --allow-counter-rollback

# ─── compose.cli.restore.commit (D1.6b) ─────────────────────────────
# Same 12 combinations as dryrun, each with a trailing --confirm.
# State-changing — acquires the global maintenance lock.
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode full --confirm
culvert-maint ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/docker compose -f {compose_path} --profile cli run --rm -e CULVERT_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE cli --restore /backup/* --mode full --accept-dp-reenrollment --confirm
